#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/enum-vs-dyn.md:1
msgid "Enums vs `dyn`"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/enum-vs-dyn.md:3
msgid ""
"Enums and `dyn` provide two different approaches to dynamic polymorphism, "
"and in many cases both approaches can be used to solve the same problem. The "
"main trade-offs between the two are:"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/enum-vs-dyn.md:7
msgid ""
"Enums make \"downcasting\" to a subtype easy via pattern matching. "
"Downcasting is possible with `dyn` but is more cumbersome."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/enum-vs-dyn.md:9
msgid ""
"`dyn` allows for downstream code to introduce new types, whereas enums do "
"not."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/enum-vs-dyn.md:13
msgid ""
"When deciding whether to use an enum or `dyn`, there are two questions to "
"ask:"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/enum-vs-dyn.md:15
msgid ""
"Do I need to be able to downcast to the concrete subtype? Or do I primarily "
"expect to go through a trait interface without needing to know the concrete "
"type?"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/enum-vs-dyn.md:19
msgid ""
"Do I know the full set of types up front, or do I need to allow downstream "
"code to extend the set of types I will be handling?"
msgstr ""
